course: dictionary
lesson: 14584
title: Planted: past form and meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Planted is the past form of plant. Plant is what you do now, and planted is what was already done. «Yesterday Sam planted a bean seed in a pot.» The seed was put into the soil so that it could grow.
explain: Planted can also mean put firmly in place. «She stood with her feet planted on the ground, and she would not move.» Her feet did not wobble. They stayed fixed in one spot.
explain: In stories, planted can mean hidden on purpose. «The detective found a planted clue under the rug.» Someone put the clue there on purpose, so it was not accident. Always test your meaning: if "hidden on purpose" fits the sentence, you have the right one.
fact: Planted is the past tense and past participle of plant.
fact: «Planted» can mean put in the ground to grow, as in «We planted ten trees.»
fact: «Planted» can mean put firmly in place, as in «feet planted wide apart».
fact: «Planted» can mean hidden on purpose, as in «a planted clue».
fact: A good check is to swap in another word, such as "put" or "hidden", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Ali planted 8 trees, then planted 5 more.» How many trees did Ali plant altogether? | 85 | 3 | 40 | *13
exercise: «Mia stood with her feet planted firmly on the ground.» What does planted mean here? | Hidden on purpose | Dug up | Lifted high | *Put firmly in place
exercise: Which word is the past form of plant? | *planted | plants | plan | planting
test: «The detective spotted a planted clue hidden under the carpet.» In this sentence, planted means: | put in the soil to grow | happy | very tall | *hidden on purpose
test: «In science, the class planted bean seeds in cups and watched them grow.» What was done to the seeds? | counted | *put in soil to grow | cooked | painted
exam: «The seeds were planted last week, and the plants are growing now.» Which word shows the planting is already done? | plant | *planted | plants | planting
